          "gloss": "spider",
          "definition": "The animal that spins a web, pictured through the frailty of what it builds.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "ref": "Isa.59.5",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "The workers of evil weave a spider’s webs. The following verse says that their webs cannot serve as clothing."
            },
            {
              "ref": "Job.8.14",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "Bildad calls the object of a godless person’s trust a spider’s house. In the next verse it gives way under his weight."
            }
