  "note": "The Hebrew noun names the animal. ‘House’ in Job and ‘webs’ in Isaiah supply the woven structure. Maltese uses the related form for the web itself. The final š of the Hebrew form has no secure counterpart in these comparisons. Kogan questions the proposed connection with Akkadian ettūtu."
